{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.QuasilatticeDirac\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.InformationalLichnerowicz\n\nWeak-owner operatorial Lichnerowicz test on the doubled carrier.\n\nThis file does not introduce a decorative geometric shell. It records the\nactual diagonal transport split already supported by the repo on `EndH`:\n\n- the diagonal operatorial Hessian is the symmetric metric sector,\n- the diagonal curvature sector vanishes by the owned bilinear map theorem,\n- and the second quasilattice-Dirac transport derivative is exactly that\n  diagonal operatorial Hessian.\n\nSo the current repo-native Lichnerowicz statement is an `EndH` theorem about\nowned transport operators, not yet a curved triality palace.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.InformationalLichnerowicz\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovTransport\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.QuasilatticeDirac\nopen InfoGeometry.Krein\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\n\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedRing EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedSpace ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsTopologicalRing EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : CompleteSpace EndH := inferInstance\n\n/-- The diagonal operatorial Hessian is exactly the symmetric metric part. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationHessian_eq_metricPart\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X X A := by\n  symm\n  simpa [operatorInformationMetricPartMap_apply] using\n    operatorInformationMetricPartMap_diag (E := E) (A := A) (X := X)\n\n/-- The diagonal curvature channel vanishes identically. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationCurvaturePart_diag_eq_zero\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X X A = 0 := by\n  simpa [operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap_apply] using\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap_diag (E := E) (A := A) (X := X)\n\n/--\nWeak-owner informational Lichnerowicz split:\nthe diagonal second variation is the metric part plus a vanishing diagonal\ncurvature correction.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationHessian_eq_metricPart_add_half_curvaturePart\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X X A\n      + ((2 : ℝ)⁻¹) • operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X X A := by\n  rw [operatorInformationHessian_eq_metricPart (E := E) (X := X) (A := A),\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePart_diag_eq_zero (E := E) (X := X) (A := A)]\n  simp\n\n/--\nThe second quasilattice-Dirac transport derivative at the reference point is\nexactly the diagonal operatorial Hessian generated by the connection channel.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero_eq_operatorInformationHessian\n    (V : BogoliubovVielbein.BogoliubovVielbeinBundle (E := E))\n    (D : EndH) :\n    let X := V.connectionGenerator\n    deriv (fun t => deriv (fun s => quasilatticeDirac V D s) t) 0\n      =\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X D := by\n  dsimp [operatorInformationHessian, operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation,\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation]\n  exact QuasilatticeDirac.deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero (E := E) V D\n\n/--\nDiagonal Lichnerowicz form of the quasilattice-Dirac second transport\nderivative: on the weak owner, the second derivative lands on the symmetric\nmetric sector.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero_eq_operatorInformationMetricPart\n    (V : BogoliubovVielbein.BogoliubovVielbeinBundle (E := E))\n    (D : EndH) :\n    let X := V.connectionGenerator\n    deriv (fun t => deriv (fun s => quasilatticeDirac V D s) t) 0\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X X D := by\n  dsimp\n  rw [deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero_eq_operatorInformationHessian\n    (E := E) (V := V) (D := D)]\n  exact operatorInformationHessian_eq_metricPart\n    (E := E) (X := V.connectionGenerator) (A := D)\n\n/--\nDiagonal weak-owner Lichnerowicz split for the quasilattice Dirac operator.\nThe curvature correction is present formally but vanishes on the diagonal.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero_eq_metricPart_add_half_curvaturePart\n    (V : BogoliubovVielbein.BogoliubovVielbeinBundle (E := E))\n    (D : EndH) :\n    let X := V.connectionGenerator\n    deriv (fun t => deriv (fun s => quasilatticeDirac V D s) t) 0\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X X D\n      + ((2 : ℝ)⁻¹) • operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X X D := by\n  dsimp\n  rw [deriv2_quasilatticeDirac_at_zero_eq_operatorInformationHessian\n    (E := E) (V := V) (D := D)]\n  exact operatorInformationHessian_eq_metricPart_add_half_curvaturePart\n    (E := E) (X := V.connectionGenerator) (A := D)\n\nend Core\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.InformationalLichnerowicz\n","mtime":1777199300149}